{"availability":"available","full":"bouzidanas/pynote-notebook-editor","name":"pynote-notebook-editor","description":"A serverless, zero-setup Python notebook environment that runs entirely in your web browser","category":"Developer tools","language":"HTML","stars":71,"forks":5,"created":"2026-01-18T10:06:19Z","updated":"2026-08-13T23:48:29Z","license":"MIT","branch":"main","homepage":"https://pynote-notebook-editor.vercel.app","topics":["data-","data-visualization","developer-tools","notebooks","presentation-tools","python","raective","solidjs","webapp"],"demo":"https://pynote-notebook-editor.vercel.app/","color":"#323057","ink":"#d6caff","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-10T21:03:34.895Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-10T21:03:34.895Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-10T21:03:34.895Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T13:01:23.347Z","stars":71,"forks":5},{"at":"2026-10-10T21:03:34.895Z","stars":71,"forks":5}],"technologies":["Python"],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["Update 2026-07-14: Lots of new additions to multiple UI areas: - Files and Data - manage the in-browser filesystem from a side panel or dialog: upload, create folders, rename, drag-and-drop to organize, and read it all from Python (press Ctrl-. in the app) - Advanced theme configuration - new theme dialog sections for cell borders and shadows, UI borders and typography, and per-token syntax colors, with themes savable into the notebook file itself - Mobile support - responsive layout with a bottom cell-action drawer and click-to-move cell reordering for editing on the phone - Markdown toolbar…","Update 2026-02-19: Major UI component enhancements! 🎨 - New .options() method for all 10 components - cleaner post-initialization property updates with method chaining support - Layout control for Toggle & Checkbox - align (left/center/right), spaced (space-between), reverse (order reversal) - Background property for all components - supports boolean, theme presets (\"primary\", \"secondary\"), custom colors (\"#ff0000\"), and full CSS (\"linear-gradient(...)\") - Full reactivity for all component properties - automatic updates when prop values change - Select component - parameter renamed from…","Update 2026-02-09: Added a suite of new UI components for the pynoteui module: - New components: form, toggle, input, textarea, and more - Full integration with PyNote's theming system - Extra features: size presets, theme-based color options, border styles, show/hide functionality - Form component includes flexible layout options (like Group component) for arranging child components in rows or columns with customizable spacing - Form submission handling support Check out the updated tutorial sections: Interactive UI Part 1 and Interactive UI Part 2!"],"features":["Zero setup: go to pynote-notebook.vercel.app and start writing Python right away. No login, no account, no install.","Serverless: Python runs in your browser via WebAssembly. There is no remote kernel to connect to and no backend to stand up (or pay for).","Private: your code and data never leave your machine.","Sandboxed: WebAssembly gives Python execution a natural security boundary. Code runs inside the browser sandbox in a separate worker thread, with no access to your filesystem and no way to touch the page directly, which…","Interactive: build sliders, toggles, forms, and layouts straight from Python with pynoteui. No frontend code, and components are live objects: set a property from Python and the UI updates in place, no cell re-run."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bouzidanas/pynote-notebook-editor/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"f221d9c1feae4024edaac7d0bbb2efc7794269ea2cebff6c360835a1fda104c4","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:23.503Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:23.503Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"Update 2026-07-14: Lots of new additions to multiple UI areas: - Files and Data - manage the in-browser filesystem from a side panel or dialog: upload, create folders, rename, drag-and-drop to organize, and read it all from Python (press Ctrl-. in the app) - Advanced theme configuration - new theme dialog sections for cell borders and shadows, UI borders and typography, and per-token syntax colors, with themes savable into the notebook file itself - Mobile support - responsive layout with a bottom cell-action drawer and click-to-move cell reordering for editing on the phone - Markdown toolbar…","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bouzidanas/pynote-notebook-editor/blob/main/README.md"},"audience":[],"requirements":[{"kind":"account","status":"required","text":"No login, no account, no install.","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bouzidanas/pynote-notebook-editor/blob/main/README.md"}],"fingerprint":"f221d9c1feae4024edaac7d0bbb2efc7794269ea2cebff6c360835a1fda104c4","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bouzidanas/pynote-notebook-editor/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:23.504Z"},"overviewRepoUpdated":"2026-08-13T23:48:29Z","readmeSnapshot":{"version":1,"status":"saved","sourceUrl":"https://github.com/bouzidanas/pynote-notebook-editor/blob/main/README.md","checkedAt":"2026-10-08T13:01:23.505Z","hash":"f221d9c1feae4024edaac7d0bbb2efc7794269ea2cebff6c360835a1fda104c4","originalBytes":9458,"storedBytes":9458,"truncated":false,"searchTerms":["pynote","python","code","notebook","components","theme","built","interactive","new","options","component","presentation","browser","cell","editing","files","like","line","mode","when","app","colors","editor","execution","features","layout","markdown","note","notebooks","out","reactive","support","update","added","borders","buttons","cells","check","css","data","directly","everything","file","form","full","info","itself","look","open","other","press","property","pyodide","reactivity","release","replace","responsive","right","runs","selection","spacing","start","styling","tailwind","theming","there","toggle","toolbar","under","updates","what","where","which","action","api","autocomplete","automatically.